# Tanager over qemu-riscv64_smode_defconfig (DR-147, docs/spec/soc.md §8.1): U-Boot in S-mode at
# 0x8020_0000 after OpenSBI's fw_jump, on the device tree OpenSBI passes in a1 (OF_BOARD), with the
# 16550 console, virtio-mmio block devices and standard boot (extlinux, then EFI).
# The boot command first tries extlinux on the first virtio disk as a whole: the RISC-V's SD partition
# holds a file system with no partition table of its own (§8.2), on which distro boot finds no partition
# 1. A partitioned disk fails that try (no file system at sector 0) and boots through distro boot.
# The host tools build without OpenSSL or GnuTLS (none on the build host): no signing tools.
# CONFIG_TOOLS_LIBCRYPTO is not set
# CONFIG_TOOLS_MKEFICAPSULE is not set
# CONFIG_TOOLS_KWBIMAGE is not set
CONFIG_BOOTDELAY=2
CONFIG_USE_BOOTCOMMAND=y
CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND="virtio scan; sysboot virtio 0:0 any ${scriptaddr} /boot/extlinux/extlinux.conf; run distro_bootcmd"
